   "html_text": "Moor (1978) argues that such a duality is one of the three myths of computer science, in that the dichotomy software/hardware has a pragmatic, but not an ontological, significance. Computer programs, as the set of instructions a computer may execute, can be examined both at the symbolic level, as encoded instructions, and at the physical level, as the set of instructions stored in a physical medium. Moor stresses that no program exists as a pure abstract entity, that is, without a physical reali",
